<title>USA: MEMC to post Q2 gain after selling plant.</title>
<headline>MEMC to post Q2 gain after selling plant.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PETERS, Mo. 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>MEMC Electronic Materials Inc on Friday said it sold a California silicon wafer plant to UniSil Corp and would post a second quarter after-tax gain of about $0.05 to $0.06 a share as a result.</p>
<p>MEMC said the plant in Santa Clara has an annual production capacity of about 20 million square inches of silicon wafers, a key component of semiconductors used in electronics.</p>
<p>The company said it would move manufacturing of the products made at the plant to its Spartanburg, South Carolina, facility.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
